  "succ_0844": {
    "title": "Crassula swaziensis醉斜阳",
    "segments": [
      {
        "t": "一切权力属于原英文作者，译者不懂植物学，欢迎指正\n转载请注明原作者&译者。原文：ICN\n译者：柳下杜拉罕\n\n醉斜阳 SWAZIENSIS Schönland, 1897Section Argyrophylla\nArgyrophylla组Synonyms :\n异名：\nCrassula argyrophylla var. swaziensis (Schönland) Schönland\nCrassula argyrophylla Diels ex Schönland & Baker fil. (1902) / C. globularioides ssp. argyrophylla (Dielsex Schönland & Baker fil.) Tölken (1975) / Crassula swaziensis fa. argyrophylla (Diels ex Schönland & Baker fil.) R. Fernandes (1978)\nCrassula argyrophylla var. ramosa Schönland (1929)\nC. swaziensis fa. brevipilosa R. Fernandes (1978)\nC. swaziensis ssp. brachycarpa R. Fernandes (1978)\nC. swaziensis var. guruensis R. Fernandes (1978).Distribution and ecology\n分布及生态Growing usually in rock crevices often in exposed positions, from northern Zimbabwe through the mountainous parts of Transvaal, eastern Swaziland and adjoining northern Natal.\n通常生长在裸露的岩石缝中，从北部的津巴布韦经过德兰士瓦多山地区，斯威士兰东部和毗邻的北纳塔尔。Short description (based on Tölken)\n简短描述（基于Tölken）Perennial plants with short erect or decumbent branches up to 25 cm long, slightly woody, with terminal leaf rosettes.\n多年生植物，枝条短直立或外倾，长25厘米，稍木质，终端叶莲座状。Leaves : 2 – 5 (-7) cm long, obovate, rarely oblanceolate, usually rounded, dorsiventrally compressed and slightly convex on both sides, covered with spreading hairs, rarely glabrous, marginal cilia becoming shorter towards leaf base; colour green, grey-green to greyish brown; old leaves persistent.\n叶：2-5（-7）厘米，倒卵形，很少倒披针形，通常为圆形，背面扁，两侧稍凸，被平展的毛，很少无毛，边缘纤毛变短于叶基部；绿色，灰绿色至灰褐色；老叶持久不落。Inflorescence : a terminal flat-topped thyrse with a number of dense dichasia; peduncle (2-) 4 – 10 (-12) cm long; bracts shortly oblong–triangular, apex rounded.\n花序：终端平顶聚伞圆锥花序及大量密集的聚伞花序；花序梗（2）4-10（-12）厘米；苞片短椭圆形至三角形，先端圆形。Flowers : almost sessile; corolla tubular; sepals 1,5 – 2,5 mm long, oblong-triangular, usually bluntly acute, glabrous or covered with spreading hairs and/or marginal cilia, fleshy, green; petals 3 – 5 mm long, oblong to oblong-oblanceolate, acute, with more or less distinct dorsal appendage, tips recurved, white, becoming cream, often tinged pink in bud; anthers yellow to brown.\n花：近无柄；花冠管状；萼片1.5-2,5毫米长，长圆状三角形，通常具钝尖，具平展的毛和或边缘纤毛，肉质，绿色无毛或被毛；花瓣3–长5毫米，长圆形到长圆状披针形，急尖，具有更多或更少的不同的背附属物，顶部下弯，白色，成为霜状，花蕾通常微染粉色，花药黄色到棕色。\n\nCrassula swaziensis from Magaliesburg Mountains :"
      },
      {
        "i": "https://pub-8b26014aee2c44c18d82a5187d985187.r2.dev/images/succ_ebc1ed1d4be9.png"
      },
